      "en": "The **test pyramid**: at the base many unit tests (milliseconds, no network), in the middle fewer integration tests (a real database, a fake API), and at the top a few **end-to-end test** cases (the whole system, webhook → n8n → DB → message). Each layer catches a kind of bug; an inverted pyramid (all e2e) = slow and brittle."
